.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_review-results.md:7:1. Concurrent EAGAIN progress is not serialized. LibSSH2NetworkBridge.service snapshots outbound bytes, awaits writeSome, then removes bytes. Actor reentrancy plus upload async stdout/stderr and writes allow multiple service calls at once, so the same bytes can be written twice or removed inconsistently. Suspended channel operations also retain raw channel pointers while cancel/reset/close can free them, creating a use-after-free path. No per-stream pending-read enforcement or operation generation protects this lifetime. Evidence: LibSSH2Bridge.swift lines 72-104; LibSSH2Transport.swift lines 340-364, 639-666, 687-785, 847-889.
