.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-2ny6z4/TASK-260715-2ny6z4_inputs.md:1:Record the SSHTransport CONFORMANCE contract that BOTH engine adapters (ReluxNIOSSH fork via TASK-260715-nzdzv3; libssh2 via 1af33i/1ozsb6) must satisfy so they are interchangeable behind the ReluxTunnelCore SSHTransport boundary (TASK-260715-2nfz7w). INPUTS: TASK-260715-28ok1k audit — SwiftNIO SSH has NO public per-channel window setter/observer (16 MiB internal target) and _rekey() is internal (fork must expose both); libssh2 exposes per-channel windows publicly (channel_open_ex / window_read_ex / receive_window_adjust2) but has NO client-initiated rekey threshold (adapter must schedule rekey manually); NIOSSH has no RSA host keys, libssh2 has RSA-SHA2. .spec/ssh-transport.md, ADR-005 (direct-tcpip + exec), ADR-006 (exec-stdin upload, NO SFTP), ADR-014 (selection OPEN). DELIVER the conformance contract: connect + MANDATORY host-key verification before user auth (ed25519/ecdsa/rsa fingerprint + changed-key stop policy per security-privacy.md); openDirectTCPIP; openExecChannel; upload via exec-stdin; PER-CHANNEL WINDOW interface (settable initial window, observable remaining, explicit cap — required of BOTH adapters; matches audit E-WINDOW); REKEY interface (client-initiated by byte/time threshold — required of BOTH); keepalive; channel close/cancel/error semantics; concurrency expectation (hundreds..1000 channels). Define the conformance TEST MATRIX both adapters run (audit E-ALGO/E-HOSTAUTH/E-CHANNELS/E-SCALE/E-WINDOW/E-REKEY) so TASK-260715-2d3g5e implements ONE suite against BOTH. Keep the engine INJECTABLE; do NOT select it (that is 1gjxer). Contract doc only.
