   154	  wait in a bounded, cancellable open queue and consume their existing
   155	  channel-open deadline. They are never silently opened on another lane.
   156	- Existing channels remain logically valid during `rekeying`. Reads/writes MAY
   157	  suspend behind engine KEX processing, but all adapter-owned read/write buffers
   158	  remain within their configured bounds and payload bytes are neither lost,
   159	  duplicated, nor reordered.
   160	- A connection-fatal error stops new work, fails all pending operations with the
   161	  same connection scope/cause, and enters teardown exactly once.
   162	- `close` is idempotent from every state. It rejects new work, cancels timers and
   163	  pending opens, asks channels to close, enforces the injected close grace
   164	  deadline, force-releases remaining engine resources, closes the socket, and
   165	  returns only after ownership counts are zero. Caller cancellation does not
